{
  "Name": "OpenEMR 4.1.1 Patch 14 SQLi Privilege Escalation Remote Code Execution",
  "Description": "This module exploits a vulnerability found in OpenEMR version 4.1.1 Patch 14 and lower. When logging in as any non-admin user, it's possible to retrieve the admin SHA1 password hash from the database through SQL injection. The SQL injection vulnerability exists in the \"new_comprehensive_save.php\" page. This hash can be used to log in as the admin user. After logging in, the \"manage_site_files.php\" page will be used to upload arbitrary code.",
